      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name} To give input on this, the public avatars (therefore I cannot fix them if it is an avi issue) I use sometimes have issues with the chatbox loading in at the appropriate height. It's then difficult to walk someone through the menu with a chatbox that is floating within the avatar to remedy this. If a 'reload avatar' button was common knowledge as a 'cureall' first troubleshooting step this may be a quick QOL fix for user error or other mishaps, and perhaps prevent creation of misunderstood Canny bug reports.\n\nTo *Corkie: Would said button be functionally different than doing the whole 'Hide avatar' 'Show Avatar' process to un-break someone's avatar loading in incorrectly? From my experience this has been the fix you are looking for no?",
